          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice O'Connor asked whether Congress meant to define felon\u2011in\u2011possession statutes broadly."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned why Congress included language about misdemeanors if the text reads a certain way."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked about the extent to which Congress discussed changes and reasons for them in the consolidation of sections."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked which case best interprets the word \u201cany\u201d as the Court should."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether \u201cany court\u201d has ever been used by Congress to include foreign courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens posed three possible ways to determine the meaning of \u201ccourt\u201d: judicial legislation, executive action, or legislative action."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec48348a8e17-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked if someone in the Justice Department could amend the form to include foreign convictions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec48348a8e1766903832cdf6a61bc00ac0680d626b1637c6090d649b1b7b9c5c",
            "evidence_ids": [
